  "details": "Recently VRChat silently added a detailed menu for editing your avatar's description. It says that it's made for the \"Avatar Marketplace in VRChat\". There HAS to be a checking phase for when you upload an avatar there.\n\nWhy is it important?\n\nFor example, a new player who doesn't know about places like Booth, Gumroad and others found a nice avatar at the Marketplace. And buys it TWICE the price without realizing that this is not the original, and that someone basically, stole his money one way or another.\n\nFor example the \"Rusk\" avatar.\n\nA lot of people love the base Rusk from Booth.\n\nThe original costs 33$. But someone else, can buy the Rusk from Booth. And then put it into the Market place for 50$!\n\nThere HAS to be a moderation. I would love to hear some more information about how it will work!",
